    <string name="en_seed_prompt">Let’s make a calm, inspiring space for my next idea.</string>
    <string name="en_seed_reply">## A clearer workspace\n\nA little **lavender**, a little light. Keep the important things close and give the rest room to breathe.\n\n- [x] Glass surfaces with soft edges\n- [x] A conversation that follows your pace\n- [ ] Your next idea\n\n&gt; Good tools should leave space for thought.\n\n| Layer | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| Messages | Rich, readable Markdown |\n| Tools | Console output and code changes |\n\n```kotlin\n// Room for your next idea\nval title = &quot;Studio&quot;\nval historyLimit = 24\nHbTheme {\n    StudioConversation(title, historyLimit)\n}\n```\n\nTry **+** below to explore a long session or add another tool result.</string>
    <string name="en_tool_result">Three directions explored · Ready to create</string>
    <string name="en_notice_text">Local demo · Your ideas stay on this device.</string>
    <string name="en_code_label">A small starting point</string>
    <string name="en_code_sample">// Room for your next idea\nval title = &quot;Studio&quot;\nval historyLimit = 24\nHbTheme {\n    StudioConversation(title, historyLimit)\n}</string>
    <string name="en_stream_response">## Let&apos;s shape the idea\n\nA calm workspace starts with **clear structure** and gentle visual hierarchy.\n\n1. Keep the draft in one spacious editor.\n2. Group related steps under sticky headings.\n3. Let tools explain their work through a compact summary.\n\n### A small starting point\n\n```kotlin\nval conversation = rememberConversation()\nStudioChat(\n    messages = conversation.messages,\n    onSend = conversation::send,\n)\n```\n\n&gt; You can read earlier messages while the response continues. Use *Jump to latest* whenever you are ready.\n\nThe result is one shared space for prose, code, and tools.</string>
